  "body": "Thanks @mcirsta for the fixes and hardware testing in [PR #50](https://github.com/Watchdog0x/jabridge/pull/50).\n\nUSB firmware updates now wait for Linux to grant access after the device restarts. They also use the device’s own restart timing and allow more time for the final status reply.\n\nRecovery waits for work already in progress. It does not send the firmware again while the device is finishing an update. Jabridge still checks the installed version before reporting success.\n\nIf an update started from the menu fails, the full error and recovery instructions stay visible in the terminal.\n\nThe contributor reports a complete Evolve 75 update from 2.32.0 to 2.38.0 over direct USB on USB ID `0b0e:2465`. The earlier Link 370 update on 1.2.0 needed manual completion. Unattended Link 370 updates with this patch, other Evolve 75 variants and recovery after power loss are not yet confirmed.\n\nThe separate Evolve2 40 firmware preparation problem remains unresolved.\n\nUpdate Jabridge:\n\n```bash\njabridge update\n```\n\nThis updates the app. Device firmware is updated separately from the Firmware menu.\n",
